BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Movie Screening: The Truman Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T150000
UID:697102a3c967cb4120832f42@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:He doesn't know it\, but everything in Truman Burbank's (Jim C
 arrey) life is part of a massive TV set. Executive producer Christof (Ed H
 arris) orchestrates "The Truman Show\," a live broadcast of Truman's every
  move captured by hidden cameras. Christof tries to control Truman's mind\
 , even removing his true love\, Sylvia (Natascha McElhone)\, from the show
  and replacing her with Meryl (Laura Linney). As Truman gradually discover
 s the truth\, however\, he must decide whether to act on it.\nRated PG\n1 
 Hour 43 Minutes
LOCATION:Cedarbrae\, FCCR (First-Floor Auditorium)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/697102a3c967cb4120832f42
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
