DESCRIPTION:This class provides a brief overview of techniques and tools t
 o support job hunters.\nIn this class you will:\n- Consider how to get you
 r job search organized\n- Find & explore job postings\n- Explore governmen
 t sites and services\n- Learn about TPL resources: Career Cruising\, Linke
 dIn Learning\, and Scott’s Business Directories\nPrerequisites: Mouse 
 and keyboarding skills required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1863f2f6bd012f006af00a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
